# Cloudflare Pages redirects for flockcorp.com.
# Port of the unconditional entries in frontend/vercel.json, then the app's
# routes that carry an id.
#
# Only the unconditional vercel.json redirects fit here. _redirects matches the path only: it
# cannot look at the User-Agent or the query string, so the crawler redirect
# on "/" and every conditional rewrite live in functions/_middleware.js.
#
# vercel.json "permanent": true is a 308, so this is a 308, not a 301.
/research/flock-research-paper.pdf /papers/flock-research-paper.pdf 308
/papers/flock-research-paper-full.pdf /papers/flock-research-paper.pdf 308

# THE APP'S ROUTES THAT CARRY AN ID (APP_PATHS in src/index.js): every screen
# under /app, the NFC check-in tag /checkin/<place>, and the push deep links
# /f/<id>, /flock/<id> and /dm/<id>. The build puts a copy of index.html in
# build/404.html, so Pages answers any path that is neither a file nor a rule
# here with that page and a 404 (a scanner probe is not a page view, and a
# browser still boots the app's own not-found page). These rules keep the
# routes a 200: each serves the app shell under its own path's headers.
#
# A 200 rule is a rewrite, and Pages runs it before it looks for a file, so
# none may match a file (the build refuses an output where one does). Its
# target is "/" because "/" is index.html; "/index.html" would be answered
# with a 308 to "/", and wrangler drops "/x/* /index.html 200" as a loop.
# Never a catch-all ("/* / 200"): that would answer every unknown path with
# a 200 again, and /static/js/*.js with the HTML shell.
#
# Not here: the app's exact routes (/app, /signup, /support...) are files the
# build writes (APP_ROUTES in scripts/build-cloudflare.js), the prerendered
# pages are files, and /i/<token> is answered by functions/_middleware.js.
# Pages does not apply this file to "requests served by Pages Functions",
# so no route that runs one may depend on it.
/app/* / 200
/checkin/* / 200
/f/* / 200
/flock/* / 200
/dm/* / 200
